te if it take longer than expect may unassign and remov from mileston expos tempor selector function\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"872f2dca8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389930076.md\", \"id\": \"532c41285ab18d1f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.315712408344829, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1108065404926129, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7938261, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389930076.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"872f2dca8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389930076.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389930076.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4478, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:33\", \"token_count\": 1509, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-REL-01]\\n\\n# Release: v1.39.0 — Release v1.39.0/v0.61.0/v0.15.0/v0.0.14\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/releases/tag/v1.39.0  \\n\\n**Author**: MrAlias  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-12-08T16:32:32Z · **Updated**: 2025-12-08T16:45:46Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**Tag**: `v1.39.0`  \\n\\n**Published**: 2025-12-08T16:45:46Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Overview\\n\\n### Added\\n\\n- Greatly reduce the cost of recording metrics in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric` using hashing for map keys. (#7175)\\n\\n- Add `WithInstrumentationAttributeSet` option to `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/log`, `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/metric`, and `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace` packages. This provides a concurrent-safe and performant alternative to `WithInstrumentationAttributes` by accepting a pre-constructed `attribute.Set`. (#7287)\\n\\n- Add experimental observability for the Prometheus exporter in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/prometheus`. Check the `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/prometheus/internal/x` package documentation for more information. (#7345)\\n\\n- Add experimental observability metrics in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlplog/otlploggrpc`. (#7353)\\n\\n- Add temporality selector functions `DeltaTemporalitySelector`, `CumulativeTemporalitySelector`, `LowMemoryTemporalitySelector` to `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric`. (#7434)\\n\\n- Add experimental observability metrics for simple log processor in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/log`. (#7548)\\n\\n- Add experimental observability metrics in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracegrpc`. (#7459)\\n\\n- Add experimental observability metrics in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracehttp`. (#7486)\\n\\n- Add experimental observability metrics for simple span processor in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace`. (#7374)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src rel 01 releas v1 39 0 releas v1 39 0 v0 61 0 v0 15 0 v0 0 14 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go releas tag v1 39 0 author mralia creat 2025 12 08t16 32 32z updat 2025 12 08t16 45 46z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z tag v1 39 0 publish 2025 12 08t16 45 46z overview ad great reduc the cost of record metric in go opentelemetri io otel sdk metric use hash for map key 7175 add withinstrumentationattributeset option to go opentelemetri io otel log go opentelemetri io otel metric and go opentelemetri io otel trace packag this provid a concurr safe and perform altern to withinstrumentationattribut by accept a pre construct attribut set 7287 add experiment observ for the prometheus export in go opentelemetri io otel export prometheus check the go opentelemetri io otel export prometheus intern x packag document for more inform 7345 add experiment observ metric in go opentelemetri io otel export otlp otlplog otlploggrpc 7353 add tempor selector function deltatemporalityselector cumulativetemporalityselector lowmemorytemporalityselector to go opentelemetri io otel sdk metric 7434 add experiment observ metric for simpl log processor in go opentelemetri io otel sdk log 7548 add experiment observ metric in go opentelemetri io otel export otlp otlptrac otlptracegrpc 7459 add experiment observ metric in go opentelemetri io otel export otlp otlptrac otlptracehttp 7486 add experiment observ metric for simpl span processor in go opentelemetri io otel sdk trace 7374\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8765f6c08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"id\": \"a1aa75b09f729579\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31108588073861476, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12746821534087824, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7395271, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8765f6c08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 52878, \"chunk_count\": 30, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:56\", \"token_count\": 15994, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-06-16T07:44:04Z\\n\\nI created \\n\\n- https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7470\\n\\n- https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6904\\n\\n- https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6903\\n\\nI think it might be also good to add some \\\"error recording\\\" recommendations in https://pkg.go.dev/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace. However, we should first clarify it on the semantic conventions side.\\n\\n>  I believe [`span.RecordError`](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/trace/api.md#record-exception) remains valuable, particularly for **non-terminating errors**. A common use case is **retry logic**, where errors occur but don't immediately end the span. This is especially relevant in the context of **custom instrumentation**, where developers have full control and can explicitly record such intermediate errors.\\n\\nThis seems not compliant with https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md#recording-errors-on-metrics\\n\\n> Errors that were retried or handled (allowing an operation to complete gracefully) SHOULD NOT be recorded on spans or metrics that describe this operation.\\n\\nCurrently, the only use case I see the only use of `span.RecordError` to use it for \\\"unhandled exceptions\\\" (which for Go can be done in the SDK) and to record multiple errors like here:\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/blob/9e39469c07651d62d1acd5155ddf9843c1b63436/instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go#L119-L124\\n\\nI do not find the semantic conventions clear and probably some work is also needed there.\\n\\nCC @lmolkova\\n\\n---\\n\\n**XSAM** — 2025-08-03T20:45:58Z\\n\\nSorry for joining the discussion late.\\n\\n@pellared I am confused about what we should do to handle errors, especially **non-terminating errors**. Should we do nothing if we encounter an error?\\n\\nFor instance, when facing code like this, do we do nothing for the error we receive?\\n\\n```go\\n\\nctx, span := tracer.Tracer(instrumentationName).Start(ctx, \\\"example\\\")\\n\\ndefer span.End()\\n\\nerr := query(ctx, db)\\n\\nif err != nil {\\n\", \"content_ltks\":